Let me reproduce this again &lt;img class=&quot;emoticon&quot; src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/emoticons/smile.png&quot; height=&quot;16&quot; width=&quot;16&quot; align=&quot;absmiddle&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; border=&quot;0&quot;/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15878625" author="sora" created="Wed, 22 Feb 2017 16:24:22 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I checked binary package but I still didn&apos;t reproduce this bug.&lt;br/&gt;
As I understand your explain, If you change the &lt;b&gt;zeppelin.server.port variable&lt;/b&gt; in zeppelin-site.xml under conf / folder, zeppelin is not work, right?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For the information, the following steps is my test for reproduce.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;1. change the zeppelin.server.port variable to 1111 in zeppelin-site.xml file.
2. run zeppelin-daemon.sh start
3. connect localhost:1111 in web browser.
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Am I missing something again? if not, it works well such like screenshot I attached.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15880303" author="adamreith" created="Thu, 23 Feb 2017 11:46:36 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;To correctly reproduce the issue you should have another service running on port &lt;tt&gt;8080&lt;/tt&gt; (In my case is Ambari sever). In this way you should notice an error opening the zeppelin home page due to the fact that zeppelin try to connect a ws on port &lt;tt&gt;8080&lt;/tt&gt; instead of using the port specified in the configuration.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15881922" author="sora" created="Fri, 24 Feb 2017 04:29:44 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hi &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=adamreith&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;adamreith&quot;&gt;adamreith&lt;/a&gt;, Thank you very much for your detailed explanation.&lt;br/&gt;
I tried to check as your describe, but I still didn&apos;t found this bug such like the attached screenshot (8080_1111_port_screenshot). &lt;br/&gt;
In my case, I changed &lt;b&gt;zeppelin.server.port&lt;/b&gt; from 8080 to 1111, and the &lt;tt&gt;8080&lt;/tt&gt; port is used by a Jupyter, and the &lt;tt&gt;1111&lt;/tt&gt; port is used by a Zeppelin. However my zeppelin works very well and I didn&apos;t see any error in homepage. So if I am right to reproduce it, I think zeppelin is working well with the configuration file (zeppelin-site.xml) regardless of another service using 8080 port.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15882359" author="adamreith" created="Fri, 24 Feb 2017 10:02:27 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I attached my screenshot. As you can see I&apos;m using the port &lt;tt&gt;9000&lt;/tt&gt; for Zeppelin and the web app try to open a ws on &lt;tt&gt;8080&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15882432" author="sora" created="Fri, 24 Feb 2017 10:43:41 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Ah, Right! Let me explain your problem.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The zeppelin web port is divided by the production mode port(8080) and web development port(9000).&lt;br/&gt;
That&apos;s why your zeppelin don&apos;t work because you set 9000 port with the web development port such like &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/blob/4c60b27c3acbdd976bf8901ef52019380bb3c334/zeppelin-web/src/components/baseUrl/baseUrl.service.js#L28&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;this code line&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Therefore, currently if you want to change your zeppein server port, please don&apos;t use &lt;tt&gt;9000&lt;/tt&gt; or &lt;tt&gt;3333&lt;/tt&gt; port.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15884171" author="adamreith" created="Sat, 25 Feb 2017 09:48:21 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Ok, now everything is clear. In this case i think that we should add that inforamation into the official documentation.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15884269" author="sora" created="Sat, 25 Feb 2017 15:11:54 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Okay, I&apos;ll update the official documentation.&lt;br/&gt;
